Chapter: BoolOrBothTrue

  cites Codex chapter Text



 Regression: Boolean `|` was compiled as integer addition in self-host's

 x86-64 emit. When both operands were True (1 + 1 = 2), a subsequent

 `&` with another True (1) evaluated to 0 (bitwise 1 & 2 = 0), dropping

 the conjoined condition. Fixed in X86_64.codex IrOr by using or-rr

 instead of add-rr.



Section: Helpers

  check : Boolean, Boolean -> Boolean

  check (a) (b) = a & (b | a)



  say : Boolean -> Text

  say (x) = if x then "ok" else "BAD"



  inv : Boolean -> Boolean

  inv (x) = if x then False else True



Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act

    print-line-uni (say (check True True))

    print-line-uni (say (check True False))

    print-line-uni (say (inv (check False True)))

    print-line-uni (say (inv (check False False)))

  end



